pairs.after_English:
- All models show "Parameters this provider supports": the effective capabilities and values supported by both the model catalog record and the call endpoint, with count limits taking the smaller of the two.
  Values recorded by neither side show "Unrecorded". This means ArcReel has not cataloged the limit, not that arbitrary values are allowed; the provider rejects anything beyond its limit.
  An image model with a reference-image limit of 0 does not accept reference images, also shows image-to-image as unsupported, and is excluded from image-to-image candidates;
- Officially listed built-in models can only be enabled or disabled under "Provider settings". Their "Parameters this provider supports" are read-only and officially maintained; changes to "Model info" are described below;

pairs.before_English:
"Change" replaces the whole item and "Restore" goes back to the original value. Models that map to no known model can be changed too;
their original values are what ArcReel infers from the model name. For video models, "Durations by resolution" follows "Durations",
and removing a resolution also removes its duration restriction;

pairs.after_English:
"Change" replaces the whole item and "Restore" goes back to the original value. Models that map to no known model can be changed too.
For image models, you can change "Reference image limit", replacing the entire limit jointly calculated from model info and the call endpoint. Entering 0 means reference images are not accepted; "Restore" returns to the original value. The call endpoint must implement image-to-image for the changed limit to be usable on that route.
For video models, "Durations by resolution" follows "Durations", and removing a resolution also removes its duration restriction;
